    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6729" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακλη-τικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fit for exhorting,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ὁμόνοιαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fit for recalling;</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀνακλητικὸν σημαίνειν,
			σαλπίγξαι</span> sound <i>a retreat,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				8.65
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.136
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκδίδωσι τὸ ἀ. τῷ Ἄττιδι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					5.169c
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				818
			</span></i>.</div>
